            <title>[LU-21063] sanity-sec test_75a: cp testf_write testfile_tenant failed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21063</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_75a intermittently fails with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;cp /mnt/lustre/testf_write /mnt/lustre/testfile_tenant failed
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow shows 13 occurrences of this signature on master lustre-reviews since 2026-09 across unrelated changes (e.g. 68693, 64784, 69516, 69323, 69265, 70051), on both ldiskfs (review-dne-part-2) and ZFS (review-dne-zfs-part-2), RHEL 9.7/9.8/10.1. Retests pass. It occurs with the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19127" title="sanity-sec test_75a: echo testfile_trusted failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19127"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19127&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (75a namespace setup) and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18569" title="sanity-sec: timeout - clients lost connection to MGS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18569"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18569&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fixes already in the build, so it is a separate intermittent problem in the tenant/nodemap part of the test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This example is from &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70051" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70051&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21040" title="conf-sanity test_66: check lustre-OST0000.osc.active failed! with many MDTs per MDS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21040"&gt;LU-21040&lt;/a&gt;), which changes import activation via sysfs and is unrelated.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
